From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soaresden <soaresden@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:28:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] kernel: don't call EKA1 entry points flagged
 KImageNoCallEntryPoint

petran and rombuild set KImageNoCallEntryPoint (0x2) on EKA1 DLLs without
static data, which is nearly all of them: every ROM DLL of the N-Gage
NEM-4 firmware has flags 0x3. EKA2L1 put all of them in the entry point
list returned by LibraryAttach, and RLibrary::Load then called each one
with the process attach reason (0) then 1. The phone cannot be doing that
(see below, CAPCODEC could never be loaded), so the flag is honoured.

Most of them return KErrNone, but CAPCODEC.DLL's E32Dll returns KErrGeneral
for that reason, so RLibrary::Load fails with KErrBadLibraryEntryPoint as
soon as a library pulls it in. Carmageddon 3D for N-Gage (Mophun player,
MOPHUN.DLL imports CAPCODEC.DLL directly) showed
"System error" at start because of it.

Mark the code segment's entry point disabled for such EKA1 DLLs, from
both E32 and ROM images. EKA2 is left as it is.
---
 src/emu/kernel/src/libmanager.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/emu/kernel/src/libmanager.cpp b/src/emu/kernel/src/libmanager.cpp
index 9a113c044..266fc05b3 100644
--- a/src/emu/kernel/src/libmanager.cpp
+++ b/src/emu/kernel/src/libmanager.cpp
@@ -207,6 +207,14 @@ namespace eka2l1::hle {
         return res;
     }
 
+    // EKA1 does not call the entry point of a DLL flagged KImageNoCallEntryPoint (petran and
+    // rombuild set it on DLLs without static data, so almost every one of them).
+    static bool no_entry_point_call(kernel_system *kern, const std::uint32_t uid1, const std::uint32_t flags) {
+        static constexpr std::uint32_t DLL_UID1 = 0x10000079;
+        static constexpr std::uint32_t IMAGE_NO_CALL_ENTRY_POINT = 0x2;
+        return kern->is_eka1() && (uid1 == DLL_UID1) && (flags & IMAGE_NO_CALL_ENTRY_POINT);
+    }
+
     codeseg_ptr lib_manager::import_e32img(loader::e32img *img, const std::u16string &path, const address force_code_addr) {
         std::uint32_t data_seg_size = img->header.data_size + img->header.bss_size;
         kernel::codeseg_create_info info;
@@ -267,6 +275,10 @@ namespace eka2l1::hle {
             return nullptr;
         }
 
+        if (no_entry_point_call(kern_, static_cast<std::uint32_t>(img->header.uid1), img->header.flags)) {
+            cs->set_entry_point_disabled();
+        }
+
         const std::size_t first = loading_codesegs_.size();
         cs->set_loading(true);
         loading_codesegs_.push_back(cs);
@@ -969,6 +981,10 @@ namespace eka2l1::hle {
 
         auto cs = kern_->create<kernel::codeseg>(seg_name, info);
 
+        if (cs && no_entry_point_call(kern_, romimg.header.uid1, romimg.header.flags_raw)) {
+            cs->set_entry_point_disabled();
+        }
+
         if (only_shell) {
             return cs;
         }
